"""resvg test suite: reference SVG renderings used by Donner's image-comparison tests.

Vendored from https://github.com/linebender/resvg-test-suite at commit
d8e064337faf01bc5a9579187a56dbdbe3eacc72 (MIT-licensed; see LICENSE). Previously
fetched via `new_git_repository(name = "resvg-test-suite", ...)` in
third_party/bazel/non_bcr_deps.bzl; vendored in-tree so the goldens are available
without a network fetch and travel with the source archive.

Layout (post-2023-05 restructure + Great Rename): tests are under
tests/<category>/<feature>/<name>.svg with paired <name>.png in the same
directory. Resources (external images) under resources/, fonts under fonts/.

The upstream `tools/` (the multi-backend `vdiff` runner), `check.py`, and
`stats.py` are vendored alongside the data but are not wired into any Bazel
target here — they are standalone scripts run directly.

Refreshed references: these tests now live in the resvg repository
(https://github.com/linebender/resvg, crates/resvg/tests/tests/). The snapshot
above predates resvg placing sideways vertical glyphs on the central baseline
at the ascent/descent midpoint, so the following PNGs were replaced with their
300x300 versions from resvg release v0.49.0 (resvg revision
66ee0dc7d787d7e0b0ab3085b7849f78838cf2ba). resvg is licensed Apache-2.0 OR MIT;
these files are used under MIT, with its notice in LICENSE-resvg-MIT. Their SVG
inputs are byte-identical at both revisions.

  tests/text/writing-mode/inheritance.png
  tests/text/writing-mode/mixed-languages-with-tb.png
  tests/text/writing-mode/tb.png
  tests/text/writing-mode/tb-rl.png
  tests/text/writing-mode/tb-with-alignment.png
  tests/text/writing-mode/tb-with-dx-on-second-tspan.png
  tests/text/writing-mode/tb-with-dx-on-tspan.png
  tests/text/writing-mode/tb-with-dy-on-second-tspan.png

From the same revision and license, both the SVG and the PNG of these tests were
replaced, because upstream quoted their `'Mplus 1p'` font-family. Unquoted, that
value is not a valid family name, and the old references were drawn in a
fallback face.

  tests/text/writing-mode/tb-and-punctuation.svg
  tests/text/writing-mode/tb-and-punctuation.png
  tests/text/letter-spacing/non-ASCII-character.svg
  tests/text/letter-spacing/non-ASCII-character.png

From the same revision and license, these PNGs were replaced with their 300x300
versions because the snapshot's references were drawn in faces outside the
vendored font set. Upstream's harness maps the generic families to Noto Serif,
Noto Sans, Noto Mono, Yellowtail and Sedgwick Ave Display, yet the snapshot's
sans-serif.png differed from its noto-sans.png (the two are byte-identical at
v0.49.0), and xml-lang=ja.png used per-language CJK faces that are not vendored.
fallback-1.png was byte-identical to the old sans-serif.png, a centered rendering
of this left-anchored text. Their SVG inputs are byte-identical at both
revisions.

  tests/text/font-family/bold-sans-serif.png
  tests/text/font-family/cursive.png
  tests/text/font-family/fallback-1.png
  tests/text/font-family/fantasy.png
  tests/text/font-family/monospace.png
  tests/text/font-family/sans-serif.png
  tests/text/font-family/serif.png
  tests/text/text/xml-lang=ja.png

From the same revision and license, these PNGs were replaced with their 300x300
versions. The snapshot's vertical.png placed its sideways glyphs 0.28 units across
the line from both Donner and resvg v0.49.0, consistent with a rendering from before
the central baseline, and the snapshot's two underline references drew 0.1em lines, twice the
0.05em underline thickness in the vendored Noto Sans post table that resvg v0.49.0
draws. Their SVG inputs are byte-identical at both revisions.

  tests/text/lengthAdjust/vertical.png
  tests/text/lengthAdjust/with-underline.png
  tests/text/text-decoration/with-textLength-on-a-single-character.png
"""

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

exports_files([
    "LICENSE",
    "fonts/Noto-LICENSE-OFL.txt",
    "resources/ub.png",
])

filegroup(
    name = "tests",
    srcs = glob([
        "tests/**/*.svg",
        "tests/**/*.png",
    ]),
)

filegroup(
    name = "resources",
    srcs = glob(
        ["resources/**"],
        allow_empty = True,
        exclude = ["resources/README.md"],
    ),
)

filegroup(
    name = "fonts",
    srcs = glob(
        [
            "fonts/*.ttf",
            "fonts/*.otf",
        ],
        allow_empty = True,
    ),
)
